// Keleustes node protocol, v1.
//
// A belai host ("node") joins a Keleustes server once with a single-use
// join token (Node.Join) and receives a client certificate signed by the
// server's local CA. Every other RPC requires that certificate (mutual TLS).
//
// Two kinds of traffic:
//
// * Node.Link — one long-lived control stream per host, held by exactly one
//   belai process (an OS file lock decides which). Presence, host advert,
//   and server→node work that is addressed to the host rather than to a
//   session: dispatches (start a session/worker/crew), jobs (GitHub or model
//   work), factory control (stop, A2A blackout). Server frames carry a seq;
//   the node acks the highest it applied and the server replays the rest
//   after a reconnect.
//
// * Sessions, Board, Jobs, Teleport — ordinary RPCs any belai process on the
//   host may call with the node certificate. A session process mirrors its
//   transcript (idempotent by entry index) and subscribes to its own inbox
//   (prompts, answers, commands) with explicit acks, so no process needs the
//   link to sync a session.
//
// Everything the server sends is remote, untrusted content on the node.
// Changes are additive only (checked with `buf breaking`).

